  </header>

  <section class="bingo-section">
    <h2 class="bingo-section__title">How it works</h2>
    <div class="bingo-section__body">
      <p>This app is built for the <a href="https://worldwide-hackathon.mistral.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mistral AI Worldwide Hackathon 2026</a>. The stack:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Thalia</strong> — lightweight Bun-based web framework (Handlebars, Drizzle ORM, multi-site).</li>
        <li><strong>Mistral AI</strong> — vision API to describe each photo you upload for a bingo cell.</li>
        <li><strong>UploadThing</strong> — client uploads images; we send the URL to our server and Mistral.</li>
        <li><strong>D3.js</strong> — card grid is drawn on the client from a JSON game state; fast load, then fetch.</li>
        <li><strong>Socket.IO</strong> — real-time updates (e.g. when a cell is filled) for a smoother experience.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Organisers create events with a list of prompts (e.g. “Team photo”, “Photo of lunch”). Players join an event, get a randomised bingo card, then tap each prompt to take or upload a photo. We run the image through Mistral, store the description on the card, and you can review everything on the admin “View all prompts” page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

